<title>UK: Next eases amid Christmas sales worries.</title>
<headline>Next eases amid Christmas sales worries.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Next Plc eased on Tuesday amid concerns the UK apparel retailer hasn't been ringing up the sizeable Christmas sales many had expected, dealers said.</p>
<p>By 1204 GMT, the shares were down 15-1/2p to 547p, a five-week low.</p>
<p>One dealer said there was talk that Next would cut prices before the holiday in a last ditch effort to make up for soft sales during the last three weeks.</p>
<p>One analyst said worries about sales may have stemmed from a 3.3 million stg trade that was reported today.</p>
<p>--Debra Sherman, London newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
